<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kshaharata dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st–2nd century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Kshaharatas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kshaharata were a dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-satraps">Western Satraps</a>, of Saka origin, who ruled in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in the first and early second centuries CE. Their greatest ruler, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahapana">Nahapana</a>, held much of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nashik">Nashik</a> and the ports of the Konkan, as cave inscriptions of his son-in-law Ushavadata show. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gautamiputra-satakarni">Gautamiputra Satakarni</a> destroyed the dynasty around 125 CE.</p></div>
